WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.104 --> 00:00:03.950
This is Your cases, the home page. The yellow bar

2
00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:07.796
says the data is synthetic, and the blue label says

3
00:00:07.796 --> 00:00:10.873
the sample answers were prepared by our team.

4
00:00:10.873 --> 00:00:14.720
I have no cases yet, so I open the sample.

5
00:00:14.723 --> 00:00:17.800
Step 1 found the nine records in the

6
00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:20.493
sample case. I press Draft the timeline.

7
00:00:20.497 --> 00:00:24.343
In this demo the summaries and warnings were prepared by

8
00:00:24.343 --> 00:00:28.189
our team ahead of time. They were not written by

9
00:00:28.189 --> 00:00:32.035
an AI just now, and nothing is sent to an

10
00:00:32.035 --> 00:00:35.881
AI while this demo runs. Nineteen timeline items and four

11
00:00:35.881 --> 00:00:38.959
bill amounts are ready for me to check.

12
00:00:38.959 --> 00:00:42.036
Step 2 shows one item at a time.

13
00:00:42.036 --> 00:00:45.498
On the left is the record, with the quoted

14
00:00:45.498 --> 00:00:48.959
words highlighted. On the right is the line to

15
00:00:48.959 --> 00:00:49.344
check.

16
00:00:49.346 --> 00:00:53.192
Three checks stand between a line and the letter. First,

17
00:00:53.192 --> 00:00:57.038
code checks that the quote is in the record word

18
00:00:57.038 --> 00:01:00.115
for word, and that every number matches. Second,

19
00:01:00.115 --> 00:01:03.961
a different AI model checks the line against its quote.

20
00:01:03.961 --> 00:01:07.040
Third, me. Nothing moves on until I answer.

21
00:01:07.040 --> 00:01:10.501
Under the line, a panel shows how it was

22
00:01:10.501 --> 00:01:13.963
checked: what the code found, the second AI check's

23
00:01:13.963 --> 00:01:17.039
verdict and why, and then my own decision.

24
00:01:17.039 --> 00:01:20.501
This page, linked at the top of every screen,

25
00:01:20.501 --> 00:01:24.731
explains how each answer is checked. Code first, then the second

26
00:01:24.731 --> 00:01:28.963
AI check, then me. The AI never has the last word.

27
00:01:29.041 --> 00:01:32.887
I read the highlighted words, then say Yes, this matches.

28
00:01:32.887 --> 00:01:37.118
The next item opens in the same boxes, and I can

29
00:01:37.118 --> 00:01:37.503
undo.

30
00:01:37.503 --> 00:01:41.734
This warning is tagged Found by code: a program counted the

31
00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:45.195
days. It goes in the notes for the attorney,

32
00:01:45.195 --> 00:01:49.428
never in the letter. I decide whether she should be told.

33
00:01:49.428 --> 00:01:52.889
To save time I will say yes to the

34
00:01:52.889 --> 00:01:57.928
rest. In real use I would read each one.

35
00:01:57.928 --> 00:02:01.390
Step 2 is done. Every item has an answer.

36
00:02:01.390 --> 00:02:05.621
Step 3 is the bill amounts. Code finds them and adds

37
00:02:05.621 --> 00:02:09.853
them up. I decide whether each charge counts toward the total.

38
00:02:09.853 --> 00:02:12.930
Some amounts, like this rate, are never added

39
00:02:12.930 --> 00:02:15.624
to the total. The page says so.

40
00:02:17.595 --> 00:02:20.672
Step 3 is done. The total is added

41
00:02:20.672 --> 00:02:23.365
up by code, not by an AI.

42
00:02:23.365 --> 00:02:26.442
Step 4. The letter is on the left.

43
00:02:26.442 --> 00:02:29.903
The notes for the attorney, marked do not send,

44
00:02:29.903 --> 00:02:32.980
are on the right. I copy the letter,

45
00:02:32.980 --> 00:02:34.134
then download it.

46
00:02:34.134 --> 00:02:38.365
This is the file I downloaded, plain text, ready to paste.

47
00:02:38.365 --> 00:02:42.598
Each charge line has a blank for the date of service.

48
00:02:42.598 --> 00:02:46.059
Back on Your cases, this one now says Letter

49
00:02:46.059 --> 00:02:48.752
ready. Everything here was a prepared answer.

50
00:02:48.752 --> 00:02:52.214
The AI's own results are in the evaluation report.

